  "body": "943m2 of Freehold Land - Views and a Massive Home.\r\n\r\nRarely does a property offer this much space, land and future potential in one package. Set on an impressive 943m² elevated landholding, this substantial 281m² solid 1960s brick home has been lovingly maintained by the same family for more than 60 years and now presents an exceptional opportunity for its next chapter.\r\n\r\nWith six bedrooms, two bathrooms and two rumpus rooms, there is genuinely room for the whole family - and then some. The two generous ground-floor rumpus rooms provide fantastic flexibility for teenagers, extended family, hobbies or working from home, with the potential to create a dedicated business space separate from the main living areas.\r\n\r\nThe north-facing backyard is a wonderful family haven, offering plenty of sunshine, space for the kids to run around and an ideal setting for entertaining. Mature fruit trees are dotted throughout the property, including abundant lemon and lemonade trees, adding to the established and much-loved character of the grounds.\r\n\r\nPositioned high on the site, the home enjoys partial views towards the Sky Tower and Harbour Bridge, while extensive off-street parking adds another practical advantage. And with 943m² of land, the property offers significant appeal for those looking for a future development opportunity, strategic landholding or simply a large piece of land to enjoy today.\r\n\r\nFamilies will also appreciate the range of schooling options, with the property in zone for Glendowie Primary School and Glendowie College, as well as St Heliers School and Sacred Heart College.\r\n\r\nThis is a genuine opportunity to secure a substantial family home with an enviable landholding, strong fundamentals and plenty of options for the future.\r\n\r\nIgnore the CV - our vendors have firm future plans in place and this home must be sold.\r\n\r\nCall us today!",
